00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
since apex legends launched in 2019 the  respawn team has added a ton to the game  new legends maps abilities lore you name  it with so much to dig into here are 9  things you might not know about apex  legends octane the high-energy  death-defying stuntman was first added  back in season 1 of apex but you might  not know that his origins actually lie  in the titanfall 2 speedrunning  community if you played titanfall 2 you  might remember it's gauntlet a  replayable tutorial area with a  tantalizing leader board that just  begged you to try it over and over again  cash mayo rose to the challenge  completing the gauntlet in 12 seconds  flat by using frag grenades to give  themselves a speed boost the team at  respawn were clearly impressed and  incorporated this into octane's stuntman  backstory he set the course record on  the gauntlet by using a grenade to  propel himself across the finish line  resulting in him losing both legs and if  you're wondering if cash mayo's 12  second gauntlet record still stands  it doesn't cash mayo has now managed to  complete the feat in a little over 10  seconds if there's one thing i know  about mirage it's that he loves pork  chops it's a good day to take out some  fools and be back in time for dinner got  pork chops tonight love pork chops so  much so in fact that his recipe is  included on one of the game's loading  screens andrew rayer more commonly known  for his youtube series binging with  babish made mirage's pork chops exactly  how the recipe calls for adding 15 grams  of ground cloves and an additional 15  grams of ground cinnamon and as  predicted this is unpalatable and i'm  not saying that to be a snob it tastes  like i just poured the bottle of ground  cloves into my eyes and mouth turns out  that manny hagopian the writer  responsible for mirage's recipe made a  slight error when converting it to the  metric system manny came up with a  revised recipe which babish made and  gave his seal of approval to mirage  isn't the only legend with a go-to  recipe lifeline's cookies and mad  maggie's warrior feast are also both  supposed to be delicious  back in 2020 respawn ran the grand  soiree arcade event and one of the  limited time modes let you play the game  in third person while the mode was  short-lived you can still play in the  third person in the game but only in the  firing range just by following some  simple steps the elephant in the room  with apex is that it's made by the  titanfall team it's set in the same  universe as titanfall some characters  and loadouts are even from titanfall  so how come there are no titans in the  game while the apex team has tried to  add them multiple times internally but  the titans cause balance issues that the  team hasn't found the right solution to  like how do you make a battle royale map  suitable for the giant titans how do you  account for the titan's vast health pool  while the team has gone on record to say  never say never with regard to adding  them to the game they're not on the road  map right now so titans may not have  made it to apex but plenty of characters  from the titanfall games have honestly i  could make a whole video about these  connections but here are some key ones  you might have missed valkyrie for  example is the daughter of viper you may  remember him as being the pilot of the  jerk titan that ripped off bt's arm in  titanfall 2.  valkyrie real name kairi imahara even  had fellow legend rampart use the flight  core from her dad's titan to make the  jetpack she uses for the apex games  mirage is the nephew of draws who helps  cooper and bt hijack the ims malta and  provided covering fire when cooper went  head to head with viper three legends  were previously titan pilots wraith ash  and newcastle while technically valkyrie  has piloted a titan before she didn't  complete her training to become a fully  fledged pilot octane owns a titan but he  isn't a pilot he just keeps one covered  in graffiti in his massive house  wraith wasn't in titanfall 1 and 2 but  she's got a cool link to the titanfall  games nonetheless she's from an  alternate dimension where the bad guys  from titanfall 2 actually won this ties  into her in-game abilities to be able to  hear warning voices which are her from  other dimensions and of course her  ability to use a dimensional rift to get  out of trouble while there are obviously  many titanfall easter eggs to enjoy in  apex legends references to other games  are hidden throughout for example  watson's strange attractor skin is  clearly a reference to samus from  metroid even down to the teal braces  mimicking samus's arm cannon krypto's  devil's advocate skin is a devil may cry  reference with the red coat and black  shirt looking a hell of a lot like  dante's usual get up pathfinder has a  banner pose called for the birds where  he gets attacked by a raven clearly an  ode to overwatch's bastion who has a  bird friend named ganymede it even  translates to weapons the mastiff has a  legendary skin called warp zone the name  itself is a reference to shortcuts from  super mario bros but the skin is teeming  with references to video games from nez  buttons and cartridge slot to a usb  connector and even a little screen now  while this character looks like a little  mega man it was actually confirmed by  apex senior producer josh medina to be  pixel jack cooper from titan tunes a  titanfall cartoon series made by respawn  animator muay para back at the 2019 game  awards mirage appeared in a video call  with host jeff keeley to announce that  year's winter event mirage's hollow day  bash tell me tell me did i already win  for best all-around competitor in a  battle royale based on skills but mostly  good looks  that is such a specific award as i told  you on twitter does not exist while it  may have looked like it was pre-recorded  and made specifically for the show it  was actually done live mirage's actor  roger craig smith was decked in a  performance capture outfit and was  speaking to jeff who was on stage at the  microsoft theater across the street the  stunt was a collaboration between  respawn and a creative technology studio  called the mill where they utilized  real-time rendered shooting tech to  shoot and animate the skit here's a  weird one that you might not know many  of the legends may look spry and  energetic but several of them are  actually over 100 years old horizon for  example is 37 but she was trapped in a  black hole for a few decades making her  roughly 125 years old ash is 121 and  also spent a few years with her head  shattered in another dimension but  that's a story for a different video and  revenant is an astonishing 313.  the youngest legend is rampart she's  only 21. okay this one's cheating  because it's a titanfall easter egg but  an apex dev helped bring it to light so  i'm counting it here a titanfall 2  easter egg went unnoticed for over five  years until respawn's narrative  historian david bartle dropped a couple  of hints on his twitter account as to  its location turns out in titanfall 2's  infamous time travelling effect and  cause mission if you time swapped 88  times outside a certain door the room  changes into a  weird one where a dead soldier's body  lies on the floor while another is  doing the splits between two kitchen  countertops  definitely a weird one but one that  remained hidden for an awfully long time  it was the creation of respawn senior  designer jake keating so there you have  it nine things you may not know about  apex legends for more on the game make  sure you check out jordan's weekly  column hot drop over on gamespot.com or  subscribe to the channel for more  features like this one if you've got any  apex tidbits drop them in the comments  below or come find me on twitter i'm at  lucy james games catch you next time
 

